# ArduPlane SITL parameters for standard_vtol: sim_vehicle.py -v ArduPlane -f quadplane --model JSON:<host> --add-param-file=<this>.
# Self-contained: with --model JSON the binary finds no frame defaults of its own, so quadplane.parm is not loaded.
# What the frame, the outputs and the flight envelope are; everything else is ArduPlane's own default.
Q_ENABLE 1
Q_FRAME_CLASS 1
Q_FRAME_TYPE 1
Q_MAV_TYPE 22

# The airframe's envelope: 10 m/s minimum, 15 cruise, 20 top. ArduPlane leaves VTOL above AIRSPEED_MIN and assists
# below Q_ASSIST_SPEED, which arming refuses to see at zero.
ARSPD_USE 1
AIRSPEED_MIN 10
AIRSPEED_CRUISE 15
AIRSPEED_MAX 20
Q_ASSIST_SPEED 8

# Controls.xml channels 0-3 are the lift rotors in ArduPilot's quad-X order (front-right, rear-left, front-left,
# rear-right), 4 the pusher, 5-7 the left elevon, right elevon and elevator. ArduPlane's default puts the plane
# surfaces on 1-4 and the rotors on 5-8; left as is, two rotors sit at half throttle before the vehicle is armed.
SERVO1_FUNCTION 33
SERVO2_FUNCTION 34
SERVO3_FUNCTION 35
SERVO4_FUNCTION 36
SERVO5_FUNCTION 70
SERVO6_FUNCTION 4
SERVO7_FUNCTION 4
SERVO8_FUNCTION 19

# Both elevons deflect trailing-edge up on a positive command, so the left one rolls left where ArduPilot's
# positive aileron is a roll to the right. The elevator's positive is nose up on both sides.
SERVO6_REVERSED 1

# The full PWM span: the simulator reads the pusher as (PWM - 1000) / 1000 and the surfaces as (PWM - 1500) / 500,
# and ArduPilot's default 1100..1900 would trim a fifth off every travel. The rotors already span 1000..2000
# (Q_M_PWM_MIN/MAX).
SERVO5_MIN 1000
SERVO5_MAX 2000
SERVO6_MIN 1000
SERVO6_MAX 2000
SERVO7_MIN 1000
SERVO7_MAX 2000
SERVO8_MIN 1000
SERVO8_MAX 2000
